## 1. Is the experiment trustworthy?

- **Sample ratio:** {{ "{:,}".format(r.srm.observed[0]) }} control / {{ "{:,}".format(r.srm.observed[1]) }} treated in the {{ "{:,}".format(r.n_rows) }}-row sample, tested against the documented {{ (1 - r.config.designed_treatment_share) | pct(0) }}/{{ r.config.designed_treatment_share | pct(0) }} split: p = {{ r.srm.p_value | pval }}, **{{ "pass" if r.srm.passed else "FAIL" }}**.
- **Feature balance:** max |SMD| across the 12 features = {{ r.balance_max_abs_smd | num }}: **{{ "pass" if r.balance_max_abs_smd < 0.1 else "FAIL" }}**.
- **Treatment is assignment, not exposure:** only {{ r.exposure_rate_treated | pct(1) }} of treated users were actually exposed to an ad. Every effect here is an intent-to-treat effect of *being eligible for* ads.

